public with sharing class ContactLookupAction {

    @InvocableMethod(
        label='Find Contact by Email',
        description='Looks up an existing Contact by email address, matching case-insensitively and returning the earliest-created contact when duplicates exist.',
        category='Contacts'
    )
    public static List<Result> find(List<Request> requests) {

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // 1. Collect distinct, trimmed, non-blank emails from the batch
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        Set<String> emailSet = new Set<String>();
        for (Request req : requests) {
            if (req.email != null) {
                String trimmed = req.email.trim();
                if (String.isNotBlank(trimmed)) {
                    emailSet.add(trimmed);
                }
            }
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // 2. Single bulk-safe SOQL query (max 1 per invocable call)
        //    • Email comparison is case-insensitive in SOQL.
        //    • ORDER BY CreatedDate ASC so the first row for a given
        //      email is the earliest-created contact.
        //    • WITH USER_MODE enforces FLS + record-level sharing
        //      for the running (Flow) user.
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        Map<String, Id> emailToContactId = new Map<String, Id>();

        if (!emailSet.isEmpty()) {
            List<Contact> contacts = [
                SELECT Id, Email
                FROM Contact
                WHERE Email IN :emailSet
                WITH USER_MODE
                ORDER BY CreatedDate ASC
            ];

            for (Contact c : contacts) {
                // Normalise to lowercase for case-insensitive map key
                String key = c.Email.toLowerCase();
                // First occurrence wins → earliest CreatedDate
                if (!emailToContactId.containsKey(key)) {
                    emailToContactId.put(key, c.Id);
                }
            }
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // 3. Build one Result per Request, preserving input order
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        List<Result> results = new List<Result>(requests.size());

        for (Request req : requests) {
            Result res = new Result();

            String trimmed = req.email != null ? req.email.trim() : null;

            if (String.isNotBlank(trimmed)) {
                String key = trimmed.toLowerCase();
                Id matchedId = emailToContactId.get(key);
                if (matchedId != null) {
                    res.contactId = matchedId;
                    res.found     = true;
                } else {
                    res.contactId = null;
                    res.found     = false;
                }
            } else {
                // null, blank, or whitespace-only email
                res.contactId = null;
                res.found     = false;
            }

            results.add(res);
        }

        return results;
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Inner classes for Flow invocable variables
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    public class Request {
        @InvocableVariable(
            label='Email',
            description='Email address to search for (case-insensitive)',
            required=true
        )
        public String email;
    }

    public class Result {
        @InvocableVariable(
            label='Contact Id',
            description='Id of the matching Contact, or null if not found'
        )
        public Id contactId;

        @InvocableVariable(
            label='Found',
            description='True when a Contact with the given email exists'
        )
        public Boolean found;
    }
}
```

**Design notes:**

| Concern | How it's addressed |
|---|---|
| **One SOQL per call (up to 200 requests)** | All emails are collected into a `Set<String>` first; a single `WHERE Email IN :emailSet` query fetches every candidate contact at once. |
| **Case-insensitive matching** | SOQL `Email IN` is already case-insensitive for the standard `Email` field. The map key (`toLowerCase()`) on both sides of the lookup guarantees a match even when the stored email and the input differ in case. |
| **Trimmed input** | `String.trim()` is applied before lookup and before adding to the SOQL set. |
| **Earliest `CreatedDate` wins** | `ORDER BY CreatedDate ASC` + the `containsKey` guard in the loop means the *first* (oldest) contact for each email is kept. |
| **Sharing / FLS** | `WITH USER_MODE` in the SOQL enforces both record-level sharing **and** field-level security for the running Flow user. `with sharing` on the class declaration adds a second layer of record-level enforcement. |
| **Order & count guarantee** | The result list is built by iterating the original `requests` list; `results.add()` appends in the same order, and one `Result` is produced per `Request`. |
| **Bulk safety** | No SOQL inside loops; all lookups go through a `Map`. The method is fully bulk-safe for the 200-interview batch that Flow sends. |

