```apex
public with sharing class AccountOnboardingService {

    public static List<Account> createAccountsWithContacts(Map<String, List<String>> contactLastNamesByAccountName) {
        if (contactLastNamesByAccountName == null || contactLastNamesByAccountName.isEmpty()) {
            return new List<Account>();
        }

        // Create a single Unit of Work that knows both object types.
        // Listing Account before Contact ensures the correct DML order
        // (parent inserted before child).
        fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow = new fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork(
            new List<Schema.SObjectType>{ Schema.SObjectType.Account, Schema.SObjectType.Contact }
        );

        List<Account> newAccounts = new List<Account>();

        for (String accountName : contactLastNamesByAccountName.keySet()) {
            Account acct = new Account(Name = accountName);
            uow.registerNew(acct);
            newAccounts.add(acct);

            List<String> lastNames = contactLastNamesByAccountName.get(accountName);
            if (lastNames != null) {
                for (String lastName : lastNames) {
                    Contact cont = new Contact(LastName = lastName);
                    uow.registerNew(cont);
                    // registerRelationship tells the UoW to populate the
                    // AccountId lookup on the Contact once the Account is inserted.
                    uow.registerRelationship(acct, cont);
                }
            }
        }

        // Single DML transaction for all Accounts and Contacts – bulk-safe.
        uow.commitWork();

        // After commitWork the in-memory records have their Ids populated.
        return newAccounts;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | Approach |
|---|---|
| Bulk-safety | All records go through **one** `commitWork()`, producing a single DML for Accounts and a single DML for Contacts—no per-record DML inside loops. |
| Parent-child linkage | `registerRelationship(acct, cont)` lets the Unit of Work set `Contact.AccountId` automatically after the Account insert, so no manual Id assignment is needed. |
| DML ordering | Passing `Account.SObjectType` **before** `Contact.SObjectType` in the `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork` constructor guarantees the parent is inserted first. |
| Null / empty input | Guard clause returns an empty list immediately—no UoW is created, no DML executes. |
| Security | `with sharing` enforces org-level sharing rules in the service layer. |

