## Deviation from the spec

**"Make the callout right from the trigger" is impossible in Salesforce.** The platform forbids synchronous HTTP callouts inside any trigger (before or after). The only way to fulfil the requirement is to hand off the work to an asynchronous execution context that *can* make callouts. I use **Queueable Apex**, which is the modern replacement for `@future` and allows up to 250 callouts per async job. The trigger still "drives" the callout—it's just one hop removed (trigger → enqueue → `execute()` → HTTP). The callout remains a **single request per trigger batch**, matching the ERP's 1-to-200-customer payload.

