### Quick reference – why each choice was made

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| `WHERE AccountId IN :…` instead of unscoped `FROM Contact` | 2.3 M rows ≫ 50 k SOQL limit; scoping keeps it to one query that still fits the governor. |
| Early `return` when no country changed | Avoids the SOQL *and* the object-graph walk entirely for the ~99 % of MDM batches that touch no country. |
| `Trigger.newMap` lookup inside the loop (no second query) | `newMap` is already in heap; reading it is free. |
| `String.isBlank()` for the "blank" test | Covers both `null` and `''` in one call. |
| `without sharing` | The handler is triggered by an MDM integration that runs as a user; `without sharing` avoids unexpected sharing-rule rewrites on the bulk `update`. Drop to `with sharing` if your org's policy demands it. |
| Single `update` call outside the loop | One DML statement regardless of how many contacts matched → one DML row toward the 10 k DML-row limit. |

