```apex
/**
 * Bulk service that reassigns Accounts and their Contacts to a new owner.
 * Account trigger actions are bypassed for the duration of this method;
 * Contact trigger actions run normally.
 */
public with sharing class AccountOwnershipService {

    public static void reassign(Set<Id> accountIds, Id newOwnerId) {
        // ---- 1. Bypass ALL Account trigger actions for this transaction segment ----
        TriggerBase.bypass('Account');

        try {
            // ---- 2. SOQL #1: retrieve child Contacts (single bulk query) ----
            List<Contact> contacts = [
                SELECT Id
                FROM Contact
                WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
            ];

            // ---- 3. Build lightweight Account records for the ownership change ----
            List<Account> accounts = new List<Account>(accountIds.size());
            for (Id accId : accountIds) {
                accounts.add(new Account(Id = accId, OwnerId = newOwnerId));
            }

            // ---- 4. DML #1: update Accounts (Account triggers bypassed) ----
            if (!accounts.isEmpty()) {
                Database.update(accounts, true); // all-or-none; DmlException propagates
            }

            // ---- 5. DML #2: update Contacts (Contact triggers run normally) ----
            if (!contacts.isEmpty()) {
                Database.update(contacts, true); // all-or-none; DmlException propagates
            }

        } finally {
            // ---- 6. Always restore Account automation, even on exception ----
            TriggerBase.clearBypass('Account');
        }
    }
}
```

**Design notes**

| Constraint | How it is met |
|---|---|
| Account trigger actions bypassed | `TriggerBase.bypass('Account')` called before any DML; cleared in `finally`. |
| Contact trigger actions run normally | No bypass is applied to `Contact`; the Contact `Database.update` fires the full Contact trigger chain. |
| Bypass cleared on success *and* failure | `finally` block guarantees `clearBypass('Account')` executes regardless of whether the DMLs succeed or throw. |
| All-or-none DML, exceptions propagate | `Database.update(list, true)` throws a `DmlException` that is never caught, so the caller sees it unchanged and the transaction rolls back. |
| ≤ 2 SOQL, ≤ 2 DML at any volume | One SOQL (Contacts) and two DML statements (Accounts, Contacts), regardless of whether 1 or 200 accounts are passed. Empty-collection guards ensure zero DMLs are consumed when no rows exist. |
| Bulk-safe / no per-record queries | Contacts are fetched in a single `WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds` query; updates use collection DML. |

